From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henri Chain <henri@henri-chain.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 00:47:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] 9664: x86.opinion: offer the gcc compiler spec for x86 PE

PeLoader correctly identifies MinGW/Cygwin binaries as CompilerEnum.GCC
and passes that as the opinion query's secondary key.
No PE constraint in x86.opinion names gcc, so the lookup misses and
getSpecs() falls back to the bucket for constraints carrying no secondary key.

That bucket already contains every x86 compiler spec, gcc included.
addQuery() rewrites each constraint into a query with no compilerSpecID,
enumerates all language/cspec pairs matching the processor, flagging as
preferred only the one the constraint named.

The existing PE constraint names windows, so gcc is present but never preferred.

A gcc-built MinGW/Cygwin PE therefore gets the Windows compiler spec,
and calling conventions, storage locations and so on are wrong unless
the gcc cspec is selected manually.

By adding the "gcc" constraint to x86.opinion, it can be selected in the
first pass and end up as the preferred cspec.
---
 Ghidra/Processors/x86/data/languages/x86.opinion | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Ghidra/Processors/x86/data/languages/x86.opinion b/Ghidra/Processors/x86/data/languages/x86.opinion
index 3542d186e2..1209b33afe 100644
--- a/Ghidra/Processors/x86/data/languages/x86.opinion
+++ b/Ghidra/Processors/x86/data/languages/x86.opinion
@@ -7,6 +7,10 @@
         <constraint primary="334"   processor="x86"     endian="little" size="32" />
         <constraint primary="34404" processor="x86"     endian="little" size="64"	variant="default" />
       </constraint>
+      <constraint compilerSpecID="gcc">
+        <constraint primary="332"   secondary="gcc" processor="x86" endian="little" size="32" />
+        <constraint primary="34404" secondary="gcc" processor="x86" endian="little" size="64"	variant="default" />
+      </constraint>
       <constraint compilerSpecID="clangwindows">
         <constraint primary="332"   secondary="clang" processor="x86" endian="little" size="32" />
         <constraint primary="333"   secondary="clang" processor="x86" endian="little" size="32" />
